---
description: Environment variables & secrets handling
globs: **/.env*,**/*.config.ts,**/config/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- All env vars validated at startup against a schema (e.g. zod) — the app must fail fast with a clear message if a required var is missing or malformed, not fail later at runtime in some unrelated code path.
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, connection strings, or tokens in code — always via env vars.
- `.env` is never committed; `.env.example` is kept up to date with every var the app actually needs (placeholder values only, never real secrets).
- Never print or log full values that look like secrets (keys, tokens, passwords, connection strings) — mask or omit them in logs and error messages.
- Different environments (dev/staging/prod) use different values; never share secrets across environments.
